  "reading": {
   "title": "A busy Saturday at the market",
   "text": "It is Saturday morning, and Hafsa is at the supermarket. She is pushing a cart down aisle three. She is looking for rice, but she can't find it. Right now, she is reading the signs.\n\nSuddenly her phone rings. It is Emre. \"Mom, where are you?\" he asks. \"I'm at the supermarket,\" Hafsa answers. \"I'm buying food for dinner. What are you doing?\" Emre says, \"I'm watching a movie, and Linda is sitting with me.\" Hafsa laughs. \"Please don't eat all the cookies!\"\n\nAfter the call, Hafsa sees a sale on rice. It is cheap today! She puts two bags in the cart. Then she goes to the checkout. The cashier is scanning the food. Many people are waiting in line, but nobody is angry. Hafsa takes her receipt and says, \"Thank you!\"",
